<title>USA: Sequent cites strong NUMA-Q 2000 sales.</title>
<headline>Sequent cites strong NUMA-Q 2000 sales.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequent Computer Systems said NUMA-Q 2000, introduced in mid-February, accounted for 34 percent of total product sales during the first quarter, up from 25 percent in the fourth quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>With major product enhancements -- including clusters, very large memory, and fiber channel -- scheduled to ship in May and June, McAdam said he expects to see NUMA-Q sales overtake sales of Symmetry(R) products this quarter.</p>
</text>
